-- gold-v11.sql  -  the morning check of the MACD fade e-mails on the 1-hour chart for GOLD (XAU/USD), rule v11.
-- ONE read-only statement (WITH ... SELECT) for mcp__Supabase__execute_sql. Replace the two markers START_MS and END_MS (each written once, in double curly braces, in the first CTE) by the epoch
-- milliseconds of the range: bars are judged by their OPEN time, START_MS <= open < END_MS; the Routine's day is (X-2d) 21:00 UTC .. (X-1d) 21:00 UTC,
-- END_MS = START_MS + 86400000. Nothing else is to be edited.
-- THE GO-LIVE CONSTANT IS NOT SET YET: GO_LIVE_MS_GOLD (double curly braces, in syms) is a placeholder that is replaced in src/syms-gold-v11.part at the release of
-- signal-alerts v40 (README.md v11.1); while it is there, the statement does not run. Bars that opened before it were judged by v39 (the MACD ride, README.md v9).
-- It recounts the rule macdx_12_26_9_w600_1h_fade96of120_in_v11 (signal-alerts v40, research/macdfade1h-prod-spec.md: at a closed 1-HOUR bar, the MACD line, the blue line,
-- is at 96% of the top / bottom edge of the MACD pane of the newest 120 bars and was not one bar earlier in the same 600-bar window; the FADE side: top -> SELL, bottom -> BUY;
-- the price in is the bar's close; no stop and no target) from the closed bars of the ONE stored row public.live_chart_fallback (XAU/USD, 1h; Twelve Data), and compares the
-- expected entries with public.signal_alerts (pair XAU/USD, kind signal, interval 1h, that rule id): the bar, the side, the entry against the close, one side a bar
-- (other_side), no stop or target (stop_or_target).
-- It is v8's statement (gold-v8.sql) with those changes and nothing else (README.md v11.2).
-- The row is the LATEST read: production judged each bar on the row as it was 1 to 29 minutes after the close. No user_id / event_id / e-mail is read; nothing is written.
-- Result: the same columns as pairs-v11.sql: row_type (RUN | SUMMARY | LINE), instrument, bar_open_utc, side, verdict, data (json). See README.md (sections v11 and v8).
